[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A devenv module owns strictdoc's wrapping and its grammar generation

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-STRICTDOC-DEVENV-MODULE
TITLE: A devenv module owns strictdoc's wrapping and its grammar generation
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Add a devenv module, named for the tool rather than the milestone --
ai.strictdoc, not ai.strictdocGrammar. Home-manager is deliberately out of
scope for now.

Surface:
  ai.strictdoc.enable    -- installs and wraps it in the dev shell
  ai.strictdoc.package   -- override the package, accepted as unsafe since the
                            generated option surface is pinned to a version
  ai.strictdoc.grammars  -- the intended way to configure it, and the path by
                            which this repository's own grammar file is
                            generated

Generating the grammar through this module is this repository's convention, not
a constraint on anyone consuming the published surface: a consumer may use the
module, call the library directly, or hand-write the file.

Closes the wrapping half of MECH-GRAMMAR-EXTRACT-SOURCE-BOUNDARY and settles
MECH-GRAMMAR-SGRA-NOT-GENERATED.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The overlay currently ships a wrapped environment because an invariant about
overlays not importing from packages was read as forbidding the layout rather
than as pointing at the wrong layer. The module is where the wrap was always
meant to live.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Implemented 2026-08-27, all three options live in
packages/strictdoc-grammar/modules/devenv/default.nix. `enable` installs
strictdoc plus the extraction runner, `package` carries its own unsafe-override
warning, and `grammars` is a typed attrset whose `elements` is declared with
the NORMALIZED type -- so a consumer handing raw attrsets to the emitter, which
asserts nothing by itself, cannot get past the module.

`generate:sgra` is the task that writes, and it is defined HERE rather than in
dev/tasks/generate.nix so the module references no task it does not own and
stays importable by a project that has none. It deliberately carries no edge to
generate:sdoc-grammar -- see MECH-GRAMMAR-SGRA-NOT-GENERATED for why chaining
the two would write a stale grammar.
<<<
